# Build output
/bin/
*.test
*.out

# Local data directory (SQLite DB + caches live here at runtime)
/data/
/var/

# Go workspace / vendor
/vendor/
# go.work IS tracked (it joins the server, pluginapi and pluginsdk — ADR-0059
# decision 9). go.work.sum is NOT: every module in the workspace is either local
# or already covered by the server's go.sum, so the file is regenerated noise that
# `go build`, `go vet` and `go test` do not need and that `go list -m all` rewrites
# on a whim. The Dockerfile copies it with a glob, so an operator who has one
# locally still gets it in their image.
/go.work.sum

# Editor / OS cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Frontend (web/) — Node + Vite + Playwright
/web/node_modules/
/web/dist/
/web/test-results/
/web/playwright-report/
/web/blob-report/
/web/.playwright/
node_modules/
# TypeScript incremental-build cache (local build state only).
*.tsbuildinfo

# Embedded SPA build output: the Vite build writes hashed assets here, but the
# committed placeholder index.html MUST stay tracked so `go:embed` and
# `go build ./...` work without a Node toolchain. Ignore everything in the dir
# except that placeholder.
/internal/webui/dist/*
!/internal/webui/dist/index.html

# Built Bundled plugin modules (ADR-0059 decision 10): `make plugins` writes one
# <id>.wasm.gz and one <id>.manifest.json here for every module under plugins/*/,
# and internal/bundled embeds the lot. THEY ARE NEVER COMMITTED — a .wasm is a
# megabyte of build output no reviewer can read, and it goes stale the moment its
# source changes. `make check-no-bundled-modules-tracked` fails if one ever is.
#
# The .keep is tracked so the directory EXISTS in a fresh clone: the embed pattern
# is `all:modules`, and a pattern that matches nothing is a compile error rather
# than the specific "run make plugins" failure a clone is supposed to get.
/internal/bundled/modules/*
!/internal/bundled/modules/.keep
# Stray root-level binaries from `go build ./cmd/<name>` (the tracked build output
# goes to /bin/, ignored above). `make keytool` writes to bin/keytool, but a bare
# `go build ./cmd/keytool` drops ./keytool here.
#
# ANCHORED, and it must stay that way: an unanchored `obelo` matches the
# DIRECTORY cmd/obelo/ as well as the binary, which silently untracked both
# entry points — `git ls-files cmd/` was empty and a fresh clone could not build
# the server at all.
/obelo
/keytool
envelope.json

.claude
.scratch

# wrangler files
.wrangler
.dev.vars*
!.dev.vars.example
.env*
!.env.example
